what:
frontend-tree-go-tokens: an untyped parse tag that is not a handle, so syntax_bridge::token_tree_to_syntax_node (and hir-expand's expansion parse) stop naming SyntaxNode (tree.md 'Kind tags ... Parse<SyntaxNode> for an untyped parse ... need a tag type that is not a handle'). Additive; my side (syntax-bridge, hir-expand/hir-def/mbe callers) is written against it.

(1) crates/syntax/src/view.rs, after `impl Typed for crate::ast::Macro { type Of<'t> = Macro<'t>; }` add:

/// The tag of a parse whose root is of no one kind (a macro expansion's, a token tree's as a
/// fragment, from [`crate::SyntaxTreeBuilder::finish_view`]): read it with [`Parse::root`]. Not a
/// handle: nothing of this type exists.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
pub enum Untyped {}

impl Parse<Untyped> {
    /// The parse as a `T`'s, when its root is one.
    pub fn cast<T: Typed>(mut self) -> Option<Parse<T>> {
        if <T::Of<'_> as AstNode<'_>>::cast(self.root()).is_none() {
            return None;
        }
        Some(Parse {
            tree: self.tree.take(),
            errors: self.errors.take(),
            outline: self.outline,
            _ty: PhantomData,
        })
    }
}

(2) crates/syntax/src/syntax_node.rs, in `impl SyntaxTreeBuilder`: old `    pub fn finish(self) -> Parse<SyntaxNode> {` + body; new: rename the body to `fn finish_as<T>(self) -> Parse<T> {` (body unchanged), and add

    pub fn finish(self) -> Parse<SyntaxNode> {
        self.finish_as()
    }

    /// [`SyntaxTreeBuilder::finish`] tagged [`crate::view::Untyped`], read through views.
    pub fn finish_view(self) -> Parse<crate::view::Untyped> {
        self.finish_as()
    }

`finish` then has callers only in blaze-fmt parse/stream.rs and syntax-bridge prettify_macro_expansion.rs (IDE-facing); delete it with SyntaxNode. Reply in the queue or by tmux to frontend-tree-go-tokens.
